# Defect 251, panel 192's R5, 2026-10-05: `\u{…}` is a string's, and nowhere
# else is it the escape it is there.
#
# - A character literal is its character's code, an integer, so it writes a
#   control character as its number, `27`; `'\u{1b}'` is an escape it does
#   not have, as before the escape existed.
# - A group head's string names a header or a library, and no name holds a
#   control character (panel 188): the escape decodes, and the head refuses
#   the character it writes, one message, as it refuses `\t` there.
#
# 2026-10-08, defect 445: the ESC is `unwritable_name` now, no NTFS name
# holding a byte below U+0020 (measured on the Windows box); U+202E stands in
# a file's name there and stays `unshowable_name`.

extern "a\u{1b}b.h"  #~ unwritable_name
    function f() -> i32

extern "c.h" link "m\u{202e}"  #~ unshowable_name
    function g() -> i32

function character()
    c: u8 = '\u{1b}'  #~ unknown_escape
